The introduced SPA catch-all route exposes a clear path-traversal primitive by joining unvalidated request paths to filesystem roots and serving resulting files, which is a security regression introduced in this patch. Because this can lead to unauthorized local file disclosure on GET, the change should not be considered safe to ship.

Review comment:

- [P1] Sanitize catch-all SPA path before joining filesystems — /home/wali/Desktop/AI BOT REBUILD/v2/backend/app/main.py:206-208
  The new `/{full_path:path}` handler concatenates the URL path segment directly into `public_dir / full_path` / `dist_dir / full_path` and only checks `is_file()`, so traversal payloads can resolve outside the intended web roots. Requests such as `/../../../../etc/passwd` (or equivalent encoded variants) on an unauthenticated GET can therefore read arbitrary readable files on disk instead of only `v2/frontend/public`/`dist`, creating a path-traversal/file-read blocker.
